  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The blast sends a piece of your skull flying, fragments of shot or bone penetrating into your brain. You now have a hole in your head! Enough intact scalp remains for the opening to close, but you’ll have a soft indention over the missing piece of skull forever more…</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> Pass a <strong>Challenging (+0) Endurance</strong> Test or go @Condition[Unconscious]; otherwise gain @Condition[Stunned] (3). Regardless, once recovered from either Condition you instead gain @Condition[Fatigued] (1) that will remain for a full week before you stop feeling dizzy. Roll 1d10 for long-term effects: 1-5 Frontal Lobe Damage: Roll once on the Mental Corruption Table. This does not lose you any Corruption Points nor does it count towards your Corruption Limit. 6-7 Temporal Lobe Damage: You become very forgetful and your Int is reduced by -10. 8-9 Parietal Lobe Damage: You suffer what is called expressive aphasia, effectively losing spoken speech (see under Amputated Parts - Tongue). 10 Occipital Lobe Damage: You gain @Condition[Blinded] (1) except the Condition is permanent as your ability to perceive visual input is impaired.</p>"
